{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["The sense of <b>Abram dwelt in the land of Canaan</b> is: in the rest of the land of Canaan in its entirety — that he would not remain in one place, but would sojourn throughout the whole land of Canaan, whereas Lot settled in one place within it, among the cities of the plain, for the cities of the plain are included in the land of Canaan. And the sense of \"among the cities of the plain\" is: sometimes in this one and sometimes in that one, because of the weight of the livestock. And this is the sense of \"and Lot chose for himself all the plain of the Jordan\" — for he stipulated with Abram that he would not enter the entire plain."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:28:00.070994493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}